<http://data.silknow.org/object/ac894a97-4329-35f6-9984-783b2c6fc4aa>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Buddhist priest’s robe (<i>kesa</i>) of traditional patched style. The silk has a satin weave ground, with predominantly white, blue and gold patterning wefts forming the design of bands of different roundels. Six additional patches at the four corners and centre top have a smaller scale design of flower sprays within squares in gold on a red satin ground."@en , "Kesa (Buddhist priest's mantle), green silk satin with coloured silk patches, Japan, Edo period, 18th century"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/8f758d02-3be2-3b81-a042-8ca30d577e06> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Buddhist priest’s robe (<i>kesa</i>) of traditional patched style. The silk has a satin weave ground, with predominantly white, blue and gold patterning wefts forming the design of bands of different roundels. Six additional patches at the four corners and centre top have a smaller scale design of flower sprays within squares in gold on a red satin ground."@en , "Kesa (Buddhist priest's mantle), green silk satin with coloured silk patches, Japan, Edo period, 18th century"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/ac894a97-4329-35f6-9984-783b2c6fc4aa/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/ac894a97-4329-35f6-9984-783b2c6fc4aa/dimension/2> ;
